## Agent Rules

- Local agents should read global rules first: `C:\Users\Admin\.agent-collaboration\START_HERE.md`
- Sandbox agents that cannot read local Windows paths should use this `AGENTS.md` plus the task pack as their rule source.
- Full standard repository: `https://github.com/lyosvne/agent-collaboration-standard`
- Shared commands: `:ALL` loads shared state; `:ONE` selects one owner; `:CHECK` runs read-only local-vs-GitHub self-check.
- Use GitHub branch, commit, and PR as hard sync points.
- Do not use `git add .`.
- Do not touch secrets, database migrations, deployment, or Git history without approval.
- Verify before completion claims.
- Produce handoff notes when another tool may continue.
- Use `.agents/coordination/` and `.agents/tasks/` for append-only task state if present.
- Do not run `rm -rf`, `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, `git rebase`, deployment, SSH, SCP, or secret-reading commands without explicit approval.

